  "text": "A presentation can help people understand an idea. It cannot make them experience its value. Until something works, your audience must accept your assumptions about the problem, the design, and the expected result. Every claimed benefit remains open to doubt. The prototype removed that doubt from the central claim. It didn't prove every component, migration step, or long-term saving. It proved the proposed architecture could solve the real delivery problem to justify commitment.",
